The file gnsstk.ver is a one-line file (with no line feed!) containing the
8-character git hash for the gnsstk version we wish to build against.
This hash will typically be obtained in one of two ways:

1. From within your gnsstk working copy, do:
git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD

or,

2. Find and copy the 8-character hash from the GitLab web interface,
https://sgl-git.arlut.utexas.edu/sgl-tks/gnsstk/
